1
00:04:42,857 --> 00:04:48,857
The journey begins.

2
00:09:25,714 --> 00:09:31,714
The Croods is a animation, adventure, family film directed by Kirk DeMicco.

3
00:14:08,571 --> 00:14:14,571
The prehistoric Croods family live in a particularly dangerous moment in time.

4
00:18:51,428 --> 00:18:57,428
Patriarch Grug, his mate Ugga, teenage daughter Eep, son Thunk, and feisty
Gran gather food by day and huddle together in a cave at night.

5
00:23:34,285 --> 00:23:40,285
When a more evolved caveman named Guy arrives on the scene, Grug is distrustful, but it soon
becomes apparent that Guy is correct about the impending destruction of their world.

6
00:28:17,142 --> 00:28:23,142
Grug (voice), played by Nicolas Cage.

7
00:32:59,999 --> 00:33:05,999
Eep (voice), played by Emma Stone.

8
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Guy (voice), played by Ryan Reynolds.

9
00:42:25,714 --> 00:42:31,714
Ugga (voice), played by Catherine Keener.

10
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Gran (voice), played by Cloris Leachman.

11
00:51:51,428 --> 00:51:57,428
Thunk (voice), played by Clark Duke.

12
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
The Croods is a 2013 American animated adventure comedy film
written and directed by Chris Sanders and Kirk DeMicco.

13
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
Produced by DreamWorks Animation, it stars the voices of Nicolas Cage, Emma Stone,
Ryan Reynolds, Catherine Keener, Clark Duke, and Cloris Leachman.

14
01:05:59,999 --> 01:06:05,999
It is set in a fictional prehistoric Pliocene era known as "The Croodaceous" where Grug, patriarch of the Croods, is threatened by the arrival of
a genius named Guy, who comes up with revolutionary new inventions as they trek through a dangerous land in search of a new home.

15
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
The film premiered at the 63rd Berlin International Film Festival on February 15, 2013,
and was released in the United States on March 22 by 20th Century Fox.

16
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
It received generally positive reviews, and grossed $587
million on a budget of $135–175 million.

17
01:20:08,571 --> 01:20:14,571
It was nominated for an Academy Award and a Golden
Globe for Best Animated Feature.

18
01:24:51,428 --> 01:24:57,428
The film launched a franchise, consisting of two television series, Dawn of the Croods (2015)
and The Croods: Family Tree (2021), and a sequel, The Croods: A New Age (2020).

19
01:29:34,285 --> 01:29:40,285
The film explores themes of daughter, parent child
relationship, stone age, father, prehistory.

20
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The tone is lighthearted.
